    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sukuma-wiki"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Sukuma Wiki"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is the most commonly eaten vegetable dish in Kenya. Kale is sliced thin and cooked down with onion, garlic and tomato until the leaves are tender and the liquid has almost gone. The result is savoury, slightly bitter, and deeply comforting."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use the deepest green kale you can find. Remove the thick central ribs before slicing. The greens should retain a little bite after cooking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
