      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a large frying pan over medium-high heat. Add the onion and cook for 5 minutes until softened and starting to colour at the edges."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the garlic, cumin, turmeric and chilli flakes. Stir for 1 minute until fragrant."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the tomatoes and cook for 3 minutes until they break down into a rough sauce."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the sliced kale in two batches. Toss each batch through the sauce before adding the next. The kale will wilt as it heats."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook for 5 to 6 minutes, stirring regularly, until the kale is tender and most of the liquid has evaporated. Serve alongside ugali or rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Kale is still tough after 6 minutes"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add a splash of water, cover the pan and steam for another 3 minutes. Older kale with thick leaves takes longer. Slice it as thinly as possible."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Dish is watery"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Turn up the heat and stir-fry uncovered until the liquid evaporates. Sukuma Wiki should be slightly dry, not swimming in liquid."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Greens taste bitter"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A small amount of bitterness is natural and traditional. Increase the tomato quantity to balance it. Younger kale leaves are less bitter than older, larger ones."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sukuma Wiki appears on tables from coastal Mombasa to the Kenyan highlands. It is cheap, nutritious and fast to make. In rural areas it is sometimes the only vegetable dish served alongside ugali. Kale grows easily in Kenyan soil and can be harvested repeatedly throughout the year. The dish has spread across the East African community wherever Kenyans have settled."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
